From: BangerSoul <bangersoul@antigravity.local>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/md/dm-verity-target: Permissive dm-verity mode to ignore block corruptions

On Lenovo Tab M11 (TB311FU / poplar, MediaTek Helio G88 / MT8786), factory
root VBMeta images (stock_vbmeta.img, stock_vbmeta_vendor.img, stock_vbmeta_system.img)
strictly enforce Merkle hashtrees with restart_on_corruption. When repacked
vendor dynamic partitions (vendor_stabilized.img) or Generic System Images (LineageOS 23.2 GSI)
are mounted under factory VBMeta signatures, hashtree verification detects
divergence.

Without this patch, verity_handle_err() executes kernel_restart("dm-verity device corrupted"),
causing an immediate kernel panic reboot loop upon mounting /vendor or /system.

Modify verity_handle_err() to log a rate-limited warning and return 0 (success/permissive),
allowing modified logical partitions to mount cleanly without device restart.

Signed-off-by: BangerSoul <bangersoul@antigravity.local>
---
 drivers/md/dm-verity-target.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/md/dm-verity-target.c b/drivers/md/dm-verity-target.c
index 2d9a3b680..7f5c2a114 100644
--- a/drivers/md/dm-verity-target.c
+++ b/drivers/md/dm-verity-target.c
@@ -218,6 +218,10 @@ static int verity_handle_err(struct dm_verity *v, enum verity_block_type type,
 	const char *type_str = "";
 	struct mapped_device *md = dm_table_get_md(v->ti->table);
 
+	pr_warn_ratelimited("%s: dm-verity corruption at block %llu ignored (permissive mode)\n",
+			    v->data_dev->name, block);
+	return 0;
+
 	/* Don't flood the log with messages */
 	DMERR_LIMIT("%s: %s block %llu is corrupted", v->data_dev->name,
 		    type_str, block);
